untested","path":"repository/cli/test/follow-ups.test.js","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":false,"classId":"projection-row-reemitted-without-change","classStatement":"A metrics row is re-versioned on every projection although its measured content did not change.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"workflow-projection.js:112 sets observedAt = events.at(-1).recordedAt, and :134 includes it in each follow-up row. changed() at :113-116 merges that row into the stored body and compares the result with the stored body, so a new observedAt always counts as a change. The comment at :107-108 ('Only rows whose stored status differs are emitted') and PERFORMANCE.md:222 say otherwise.","failureScenario":"Ordinary run with follow-ups: each mutating operation appends an event and projects -> every follow-up row gets a new reporting_observations version only because observedAt moved, contradicting PERFORMANCE.md ('Re-emitted when its status changes') and the code comment; store growth only, measures read latest rows and stay correct.","id":"claude-code/review-follow-up-row-reemit","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/performance/workflow-projection.js","severity":"low"},{"blocking":false,"classId":"missing-local-receipt-affected-suite","classStatement":"A test suite exercising changed code has no local receipt on the candidate tree.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"cli/test/metrics-repair.test.js:8 imports importSnapshot/reportingDatabase from the changed performance/fleet.js and uses the lightweight fixture, which now projects follow-ups. CLI receipt index 1 excludes it (`grep -v ... -e metrics-repair`). ci/portable-acceptance.sh:21 runs the full `npm test --prefix cli` under the planned 'Ubuntu 24.04/22.04 acceptance' checks.","failureScenario":"The fleet.js observation-schema change (new `follow-up` kind, followUp/followUpTracking fields) would also have to break snapshot import or repair, which is unlikely for an additive change -> metrics-repair.test.js wou