Hub remote and asserts a seed. Filed issue text is redacted of local paths, workspace and folder name, host, run ID, other repositories and followUpRedactions. The PR follow-up lines carry reviewer class text unredacted like the existing summary (low finding). The #147 reviewer-adapter files have identical line counts in base and head. Design commitments D1-D10 are reflected, and the interview, design and mandate are unchanged.","outcome":"PASS"},"mode":"full","outcome":"FAIL","prior":null,"priorCandidate":null,"receipt":{"bytes":772,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:90ec962a143c1d2340addfb7936d0431698ea6963741300efa1e2dddea506812"},"reviewerLaunched":true,"runId":"ed9ea378-6b03-4dd4-b788-46959f6b66e7","summary":"Paired boundary review (round 1, band all-non-low) of feature tb-follow-up-records, closing #148, at head c26be0b6 against base f6f421d4. The target is the same commit as the base. The implementation follows the approved design and amended spec. A new follow-ups.js derives review follow-ups on read from retained review results using the shared raise-time rule (raisedBlocking now replaces the projection's inline rule), and records dependency-scan follow-ups with their dedup key. followup.decide covers the authority rules, the policy defaults, issue filing through core.runtime.gh with marker reuse, redaction and all-or-nothing filing. Completion and release-merge enforcement, goal readiness and park, the stale ready record, status, follow-ups.md, the PR summary, metrics projection v3, measure 2/3 and the CLI are all wired. Documents and desktop mirrors are updated, and a passing test verifies the mirrors byte for byte. I found no blocking code defect. The review fails on two rubric pass conditions that the tests never exercise. (1) R1 requires a `present` disposition after `fixed` to reopen a follow-up, but the test reopens only by re-report. (2) R7 requires follow-ups.md written by followup.decide, but the test reads only the file that followup.render rewrote afterwards. Both are trivially fixable test additions; the behaviour itself looks correct on inspection. Five low, nonblocking findings are also recorded: follow-up metric rows re-emitted on every projection, two affected-suite receipts deferred to hosted CI, unredacted class text in the PR follow-up lines, and unreadable non-review results counted as follow-ups unavailable. Caveats: the read-only view has no diff, so I identified changed paths by vocabulary search, entry counts (4 new files) and line-count comparison. The #147 reviewer files (execution.js, boundary-review.js, local-agent-adapters.js), round-policy.js, contracts.js, sweep-records.js and the test helpers have unchanged line counts. Hosted CI has not run yet; it is planned after convergence."}